Version 1.0, October 2026

This is an agreement between you and the developer of Rowcast. Please read it before you
install or use Rowcast. By installing or using Rowcast, you accept it. If you do not accept
it, do not install or use Rowcast.

1. Definitions

"Developer" means Avraham Ayele, the author of Rowcast and the licensor under this
agreement.

"Rowcast" means the Rowcast plugin for JetBrains IDEs, the Rowcast command-line tool, and their
documentation, including updates the Developer provides.

"JetBrains" means JetBrains s.r.o. and its affiliates. "JetBrains Marketplace" means the
service at plugins.jetbrains.com through which Rowcast may be distributed.

"You" means the person or the organization that installs or uses Rowcast.

2. Who this agreement is between

The Developer is the licensor of Rowcast. JetBrains is not a party to this agreement and has no
duties or liability to you under it.

3. License

The Developer gives you a non-exclusive, non-transferable license to install and use Rowcast,
following its documentation.

  a) Free versions. While Rowcast, or a version of it, is offered free of charge, your license
     to that version is perpetual.

  b) Paid versions. If the Developer later offers a paid version, its license lasts for the
     period you paid for, as stated when you buy it. A perpetual license to a free version you
     already have is not taken away.

The Developer may stop offering a free version in the future. This does not end your license
to a free version you already have.

4. What you may not do

Unless the Developer allows it in writing, or the law allows it even though this agreement
says otherwise, you may not:

  a) modify Rowcast or make derivative works from it;
  b) reverse-engineer, decompile, or disassemble Rowcast;
  c) sell, rent, lend, sublicense, or redistribute Rowcast;
  d) remove or change any copyright or license notice in Rowcast.

5. Your data and your requests

Rowcast runs on your computer. It reads the data sources you set up and sends requests only to
the addresses you set up. It does not send your data, your requests, or usage information to
the Developer or to anyone else.

You are responsible for the requests you send with Rowcast. Make sure you have permission to
read the data sources you use and to call the systems you send requests to. Rowcast can send a
very large number of requests. Do not use it against systems you are not allowed to test.

Passwords you enter in the plugin are kept in your IDE's password store. Rowcast does not write
them to its files.

6. Third-party components

Rowcast includes software from other authors, for example database drivers and libraries.
Each of these components is licensed under its own terms, and those terms apply to it.
Rowcast does not include the IBM DB2 driver. If you use DB2, you get that driver from IBM under
IBM's own license.

